OL,3,GNEWSA'I thought it was perimenopause
OL,4,Abut it was incurable cancer'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mum who put memory problems, brain
OL,7,Ffog and irritability down to
OL,8,Fperimenopause was devastated to learn
OL,9,Fshe had an incurable brain tumour.
OL,11,FJane Roberts, 47, from North Somerset,
OL,12,Fsought medical advice after noticing
OL,13,Fchanges to her memory and
OL,14,Fconcentration. Instead of confirming
OL,15,Fhormonal changes, scans revealed
OL,16,Fabnormalities on her brain.
OL,18,FThe tumour is inoperable and Roberts
OL,19,Fnow undergoes scans every six months.
OL,20,FShe has since raised almost #25,000 for
OL,21,Fcharity and is calling for greater
OL,22,Finvestment in brain tumour research.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
